WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.770
In this video, you put a host into maintenance mode. Its virtual machines live-migrate to other hosts, so you can service the host without downtime.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.970
The virtual machine demo-maint is running on the host ser5-purple.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.850
Open the Hosts page.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:23.890
ser5-purple is Active. Suppose it needs a firmware update or new hardware.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.740
Open its actions menu,

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.170
and select Enable Maintenance Mode.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:38.970
Leave Force cleared. Virtual machines that can live-migrate move to other hosts. Force would shut down the ones that cannot.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.000
Select Apply.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:52.620
SUSE Virtualization live-migrates the virtual machines away and drains the host. ser5-purple is now in maintenance mode.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.030
Back on the Virtual Machines page,

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.310
demo-maint kept running. It now runs on another host.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:05.000
When the work on the host is done, return to the Hosts page,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.030
open the actions menu for ser5-purple,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.300
and select Disable Maintenance Mode.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:21.300
ser5-purple is Active again and accepts new workloads. The virtual machine stays on its new host.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:29.265
The host went into maintenance and came back while the virtual machine kept running. Next, you pass a GPU through to a virtual machine.
